      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Given that your soil pH is already 6.2, blood meal is the better choice because it raises pH very slowly and provides readily available nitrogen through the breakdown of protein. Bone meal is a slower-release source but is more alkaline and could potentially upset your current balanced pH, whereas blood meal fits your goal of correcting nitrogen deficiency without a major pH spike. Combining blood meal with consistent watering will help apply these nutrients evenly for optimal kale growth.",
